id: k8s.probe.startup
kind: kubernetes
title: Startup probe
aliases: startup, startupProbe
tags: operations, health
questions:
  - how do you probe slowly starting applications without weakening liveness?
invariant: A startup probe suspends liveness and readiness checks until the process has finished booting.
answer_30s: A startup probe gives a slow-booting process a larger one-off budget and disables liveness/readiness until it passes.
answer_2m: |
  It exists to remove a compromise: without it you either set a huge
  initialDelaySeconds (which weakens liveness forever) or a short one (which
  crash-loops slow starts). Set the startup probe to the worst-case boot time;
  once it passes, liveness takes over with tight thresholds. Typical for
  legacy JVMs, migrations on boot, and large model loads.
when_to_use:
  - slow or variable startup plus a strict liveness policy
related:
  - k8s.probe.liveness
  - k8s.probe.readiness
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/configure-liveness-readiness-startup-probes/
